Z||000001||ChopTop||08-29-2001||05:23 PM||||Yes Belltech quit producing those spindles several years ago.  I bought mine back in 1990, they are on my 85GT.  I've only seen one set offered for sale since then. Check out the pictures of the recent Lansing, MI gathering.  Forum member Tigger (bright orange coupe) installed the Street Dreams dropped spindles.  They look really great, and they are currently available.  For pics of my car with the Belltech dropped spindles you'll have to do a search for whaletail, should give you an idea of how the two compare drop wise.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroMaster88||08-29-2001||05:27 PM||||Does Street Dreams make spindles for the 88's?<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">            <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe With a new V6<BR>5 speed Isuzu trans<BR>AcCel 8mm wires<BR>rapid fire plugs<BR>custom intake with K&N filter.<BR>Soon to be 2" closer to the ground and have a turbo||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rick 88||08-29-2001||05:40 PM||||There is somebody out there making a drop front control arm for Fieros. I can't remember where I saw it though. They were offered in different drops and kept the stock springs. I believe they were sold on an exchange basis and were available for 88's as well. If anyone remembers who is doing this please post it here. <P>Rick<BR>yellow 88 GT 5-speed||||reg||3
